<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahadur Shah of Nepal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1757–1797</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bahadur Shah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithvi-narayan-shah">Prithvi Narayan Shah</a> and regent of the Kingdom of Nepal from 1785 to 1794 for his young nephew Rana Bahadur Shah. Under his leadership the Gorkha armies continued the unification of Nepal, annexing many hill kingdoms to the west, including Tanahun, and fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a>. He was later imprisoned and died in 1797.</p></div>
